{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-11675-r4494001","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Rhubarb Cake","sourcePageId":11675,"sourceRevision":"4494001","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-05-25T02:44:49Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Rhubarb%20Cake&oldid=4494001","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:18.561Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Dessert recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cake","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using buttermilk","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using rhubarb","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5446707ae8e3d3cedad40a0371c1a250e6561c9264fe9d375d345cfdffc47344","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cake recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]] | [[Cookbook:Cake|Cake]] \n\nRhubarb may be an intimidatingly tart vegetable eaten on its own, but when its sharp flavor is tempered with the addition of butter and sugar, it makes excellent desserts such as the cake recipe below.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] thinly-[[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] raw [[Cookbook:Rhubarb|rhubarb]]\n*1½ cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*½ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Tsp|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*1 cup sour [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]] or cultured [[Cookbook:Buttermilk|buttermilk]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]]\n*2 cups [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Baking Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#[[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] the brown sugar and butter until fluffy. [[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] in the egg and salt.\n#Stir in the milk, baking soda, vanilla, and flour. Once blended, add the rhubarb and stir until mixed in.\n#Pour batter into greased 9x13-inch [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|pan]]. Combine the ¼ cup sugar and cinnamon, then sprinkle on top of the batter.\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] at 375°F for 30–35 minutes.\n\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rhubarb]]\n[[Category:Recipes for cake]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using buttermilk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Rhubarb Cake","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1½ cup thinly-sliced raw rhubarb","sourceText":"1½ cup thinly-sliced raw rhubarb","amountText":"1½ cup thinly-sliced raw rhubarb","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1½ cup brown sugar","sourceText":"1½ cup brown sugar","amountText":"1½ cup brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ cup butter or margarine","sourceText":"½ cup butter or margarine","amountText":"½ cup butter or margarine","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 egg","sourceText":"1 egg","amountText":"1 egg","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ tsp salt","sourceText":"½ tsp salt","amountText":"½ tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 cup sour milk or cultured buttermilk","sourceText":"1 cup sour milk or cultured buttermilk","amountText":"1 cup sour milk or cultured buttermilk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 tsp baking soda","sourceText":"1 tsp baking soda","amountText":"1 tsp baking soda","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 tsp vanilla","sourceText":"1 tsp vanilla","amountText":"1 tsp vanilla","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 cups flour","sourceText":"2 cups flour","amountText":"2 cups flour","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"¼ cup sugar","sourceText":"¼ cup sugar","amountText":"¼ cup sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"1 tsp cinnamon","sourceText":"1 tsp cinnamon","amountText":"1 tsp cinnamon","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Cream the brown sugar and butter until fluffy. Beat in the egg and salt.","sourceText":"Cream the brown sugar and butter until fluffy. Beat in the egg and salt.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Stir in the milk, baking soda, vanilla, and flour. Once blended, add the rhubarb and stir until mixed in.","sourceText":"Stir in the milk, baking soda, vanilla, and flour. Once blended, add the rhubarb and stir until mixed in.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Pour batter into greased 9x13-in